> Is it safe to continue playing?

Yes, without any doubt.

What happened is that the lit lamp was set off when the bones file was
created. But the timer of the lamp hasn't been stopped.

So after you entered the bones and the timer started again to count
down. When it reached 0 == "when the lamp burnt up all its oil" the
program tried to put out a lamp that was already not lit.

That's where the message came from.

NetHack is a bit harsh with it's warnings. Most instances when such
warnings may be printed are not that dire and often, if saving and
reloading works, you can continue playing without a problem.

In your case not even that would have been necessary.

